==English==
{{wp}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|voyce||obsolete}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|a=RP,GA|/vɔɪs/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-voice.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|a=Indic|/vɔjs/|/vɑjs/<a:father-bother>}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪs|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=sound|:inh|enm:voys}}
{{dercat|en|itc-pro|ine-pro}}
From {{inh|en|enm|voice}}, {{m|enm|voys}}, {{m|enm|vois}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|[[voiz]], [[voys]], [[voice]]}}, {{der|en|fro|[[vois]], [[voiz]]}} (Modern {{cog|fr|voix}}), from {{der|en|la|vōcem}}, accusative form of {{m|la|vōx|t=voice}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sa|वाच्}}, {{cog|grc|ὄψ}}, {{cog|fa|آواز|tr=âvâz}}. Displaced native {{cog|enm|steven|t=voice}} (from {{cog|ang|stefn}} (see {{l|en|steven}})), {{cog|ang|hlēoþor#Noun}}, {{cog|ang|woþ#Noun_2}}, and {{cog|ang|reord#Noun}}. Compare {{m|en|advocate}}, {{m|en|advowson}}, {{m|en|avouch}}, {{m|en|convoke}}, {{m|en|vocal}}, {{m|en|vouch}}, {{m|en|vowel}}. {{doublet|en|vox}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Sound [[utter]]ed by the mouth, especially by human beings in speech or song; sound thus uttered considered as possessing some special quality or character.
#: {{syn|en|steven<q:obsolete>|reard<q:obsolete or dialectal>}}
#: {{ux|en|The human '''voice''' is the oldest [[musical instrument]] in history.}}
#: {{ux|en|Stop repeating in that stupid '''voice''' what I say.}}
#: {{ux|en|There was a slight catch in her '''voice''' as she read the letter [[out loud]].}}
#: {{ux|en|His low '''voice''' allowed him to become a bass in the choir.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare King Lear|V|iii|309|1|Her '''voice''' was euer ſoft,<br>Gentle, and low, an excellent thing in woman.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Poems|poem=Nativity|page=2|passage=And joyn thy '''voice''' unto the Angel Quire,}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=April 10, 2011|author=Alistair Magowan| title=Aston Villa 1 - 0 Newcastle| work=BBC Sport| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9446263.stm| passage=Villa chief executive Paul Faulkner had backed manager Houllier during the week and asked for the fans to get behind their team as they looked to steer themselves away from the relegation zone. <br>To that end, the home supporters were in good '''voice''' to begin with, but it was Newcastle who started the game in the ascendancy, with Barton putting a diving header over the top from Jose Enrique's cross.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260903052909/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/eng_prem/9446263.stm|archivedate=3 September 2026}}
# {{lb|en|phonetics}} Sound made through vibration of the vocal cords; [[sonant]], or [[intonated]], utterance; tone; — distinguished from mere [[breath]] sound as heard in whispering and voiceless consonants.
# The [[tone]] or [[sound]] [[emitted]] by an [[object]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|1 Kings|19|12|text= And after the earthquake, a fire, but the Lord was not in the fire: and after the fire, a still small '''voice'''.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Job|40|9|text=Canst thou thunder with a '''voice''' like him?}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|93|3|text=The floods have lifted up their '''voice'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1712|author=w:Joseph Addison|title=w:Cato, a Tragedy
|passage=O Marcus, I am warm’d; my heart Leaps at the trumpet’s '''voice'''.}}
# The faculty or power of utterance.
#: {{ux|en|to cultivate the '''voice'''}}
# That which is [[communicated]]; [[message]]; [[meaning]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Galatians|4|20|text=I desire to bee present with you now, and to change my '''voyce''', for I stand in doubt of you.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|V|vii|passage=My '''voice''' is in my sword.}}
#* '''17th century''', {{w|John Fell (bishop)|John Fell}}, unknown work
#*: {{quote|en|Let us call on God in the '''voice''' of his church.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} An [[express]]ed [[opinion]], [[choice]], [[will]], [[desire]], or [[wish]]; the [[right]] or [[ability]] to [[make]] such [[expression]] or to [[have]] it [[consider]]ed.
#: {{syn|en|steven<q:obsolete>|vote|say-so}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|II|iii|passage=''Sicinius''. How now, my masters! have you chose this man? / ''1st Citizen''. He has our '''voices''', sir.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Aeneis|passage=Some laws ordain, and some attend the choice / Of holy senates, and elect by '''voice'''.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|url=https://edition.cnn.com/2019/03/22/asia/thai-election-young-voters-intl/index.html| author=Helen Regan; Kocha Olarn| date=2019-03-24| accessdate=2019-03-24| title=Thailand's youth demand change ahead of elections
|passage=Like many of the 7 million other first time voters, she came of age during half a decade of military rule that has governed the country since former general turned Prime Minister Prayut Chan-o-cha seized power in a 2014 coup. "We have had our '''voice''' taken away for five years," she says.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251009015225/https://edition.cnn.com/2019/03/22/asia/thai-election-young-voters-intl/index.html|archivedate=9 October 2025}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} [[command|Command]]; [[precept]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Deuteronomy|8|20|text=As the nations which the Lord destroyeth before your face, so shall yee perish; because ye would not be obedient vnto the '''voice''' of the Lord your God.}}
# One who speaks; a [[speak]]er.
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|passage=a potent '''voice''' of Parliament.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Sonia Tascon; Tyson Wils|title=Activist Film Festivals: Towards a Political Subject
|passage=The inclusion of transgender '''voices''' further disrupts the homonormalization of sex and identity evident in popular LGBTQ cinema.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Katie Rogers|quotee=w:Joe Biden|title=Biden Says It Is Time to Step Aside for a Fresh, Younger Voice|date=2024-07-25|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/24/us/politics/biden-address.html|passage=President Biden told the American public in an Oval Office address on Wednesday that he had abandoned his re-election campaign because there is “a time and a place for new '''voices''', fresh '''voices''' — yes, younger '''voices'''.”|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251009014922/https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/24/us/politics/biden-address.html|archivedate=9 October 2025}}
# {{lb|en|literature}} A particular style or way of writing that expresses a certain [[tone]] or feeling.
# {{senseid|en|grammar}} {{lb|en|grammar}} A particular way of inflecting or conjugating [[verb]]s, or a particular form of a verb, which indicates the relation of the subject of the verb to the action which the verb expresses.
#: {{syn|en|diathesis|gender|[[grammatical]] voice|[[verbal]] voice}}
#: {{ux|en|The verbal system of Latin has two '''voices''', active and passive.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Drew Arlen Mannetter|title=I Came, I Saw, I Translated| page=197| passage=There are four tenses of the subjunctive (present, perfect, imperfect, and pluperfect) and three '''voices''' (active, passive, and deponent). {{...}} See 12.8 for the formation of the deponent '''voice'''.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} In [[harmony]], an independent vocal or instrumental part in a piece of [[composition]].
#: {{ux|en|The theme of this piece constantly migrates between the three '''voice''' parts.}}
# {{lb|en|Internet|[[IRC]]}} A [[flag]] associated with a [[user]] on a [[channel]], determining whether they can send messages to the channel.

