=====Translations=====
{{see translation subpage|Noun}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|voysen}}, {{m|enm|voicen}}, from the noun (see above).

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To give [[utterance]] or [[expression]] to; to utter; to [[publish]]; to [[announce]]
#: {{ux|en|He '''voiced''' the sentiments of the nation.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1893|author=w:Annie Wood Besant|title=s:An Autobiography
|passage=How often he would '''voice''' his love of England, his admiration of her Parliament, his pride in her history.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Essayes|year=1625|Of Great Place|text=Rather assume thy right in silence and {{...}} then '''voice''' it with claims and challenges.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Henry 7|text=It was '''voiced''' that the king purposed to put to death Edward Plantagenet.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|phonology}} To utter audibly, with tone and not just breath.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To fit for producing the [[proper]] [[sound]]s; to [[regulate]] the tone of
#: {{ux|en|'''voice''' the pipes of an organ}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[vote]]; to [[elect]]; to [[appoint]]
# {{lb|en|intransitive|obsolete}} To [[clamor]]; to cry out<ref>{{R:New English Dictionary|Voice|part of speech=v|X|283|3|part=2}}</ref>
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1666|author=Robert South|title=A ſermon preached at Lambeth-Chappel on the 25th of November{{...}}|publisher=William Nott|location=London|url=https://ota.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/repository/xmlui/bitstream/handle/20.500.12024/A60948|passage=It is not the gift of every Perſon, nor of every Age, to harangue the multitude, to '''Voice''' it high and loud, & ''Dominari in Concionibus''.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson Holy Grail|poem=Lucretius|page=211|passage=[L]ambs are glad / Nosing the mother's udder, and the bird / Makes his heart '''voice''' among the blaze of flowers: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|Internet|IRC}} To assign the [[voice]] flag to a [[user]] on [[IRC]], permitting them to send messages to the [[channel]].
# {{lb|en|television|film}} To act as a [[voice actor]] to [[portray]] a character.

